{
  "id": "pc-trig-04",
  "version": 2,
  "title": "Tangent and other trig graphs",
  "xp": 20,
  "tags": [
    "precalculus",
    "trigonometry",
    "graphs"
  ],
  "learn": [
    {
      "id": "intro",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "Tangent is a ratio",
      "body": "Since $\\tan x=\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}$, the graph breaks wherever $\\cos x=0$, at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+k\\pi$. Those are vertical asymptotes. Tangent is zero where $\\sin x=0$, and its period is $\\pi$, not $2\\pi$."
    },
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "What it looks like",
      "body": "Between two asymptotes the graph rises from far below to far above, passing through $(0,0)$ and $\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{4},1\\right)$. There is no amplitude, because tangent takes every real value."
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "kind": "text",
      "title": "The reciprocal functions",
      "body": "Three more: $\\operatorname{sec} x=\\frac{1}{\\cos x}$, $\\operatorname{csc} x=\\frac{1}{\\sin x}$ and $\\operatorname{cot} x=\\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}$. Each has asymptotes where its denominator is zero."
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "kind": "example",
      "title": "Period of $\\tan(2x)$",
      "body": "Compress the tangent graph.",
      "steps": [
        "Tangent has period $\\pi$",
        "Replace $x$ by $2x$: period $\\frac{\\pi}{B}=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
        "Asymptote nearest zero: $2x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, so $x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "kind": "example",
      "title": "Find $\\operatorname{sec} 60^\\circ$",
      "body": "Use cosine.",
      "steps": [
        "$\\cos60^\\circ=\\frac12$",
        "$\\operatorname{sec}60^\\circ=\\frac{1}{1/2}=2$"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "q1",
      "type": "type_answer",
      "prompt": "What is $\\tan\\frac{\\pi}{4}$?",
      "accepted": [
        "1"
      ],
      "keypad": "numeric",
      "explanation": "At $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ sine and cosine are equal."
    },
    {
      "id": "q2",
      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "prompt": "What is the period of $y=\\tan x$?",
      "choices": [
        "$\\pi$",
        "$2\\pi$",
        "$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
        "$4\\pi$"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 0,
      "explanation": "Tangent repeats every $\\pi$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q3",
      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "prompt": "Where does $\\tan x$ have a vertical asymptote?",
      "choices": [
        "$x=0$",
        "$x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$",
        "$x=\\pi$",
        "$x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}$"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 1,
      "explanation": "$\\cos\\frac{\\pi}{2}=0$, so tangent is undefined there."
    },
    {
      "id": "q4",
      "type": "type_answer",
      "prompt": "What is $\\operatorname{sec} 60^\\circ$?",
      "accepted": [
        "2"
      ],
      "keypad": "numeric",
      "explanation": "$\\operatorname{sec}60^\\circ=\\frac{1}{\\cos60^\\circ}=2$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q5",
      "type": "type_answer",
      "prompt": "What is $\\operatorname{csc} 30^\\circ$?",
      "accepted": [
        "2"
      ],
      "keypad": "numeric",
      "explanation": "$\\operatorname{csc}30^\\circ=\\frac{1}{\\sin30^\\circ}=\\frac{1}{1/2}=2$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q6",
      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "prompt": "What is the period of $y=\\tan(3x)$?",
      "choices": [
        "$3\\pi$",
        "$\\frac{2\\pi}{3}$",
        "$\\frac{\\pi}{3}$",
        "$\\pi$"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 2,
      "explanation": "The period is $\\frac{\\pi}{B}=\\frac{\\pi}{3}$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q7",
      "type": "match_pairs",
      "prompt": "Match each function to its definition.",
      "pairs": [
        [
          "$\\operatorname{sec} x$",
          "$\\frac{1}{\\cos x}$"
        ],
        [
          "$\\operatorname{csc} x$",
          "$\\frac{1}{\\sin x}$"
        ],
        [
          "$\\operatorname{cot} x$",
          "$\\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x}$"
        ],
        [
          "$\\tan x$",
          "$\\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}$"
        ]
      ],
      "explanation": "Each is built from sine and cosine."
    },
    {
      "id": "q8",
      "type": "multiple_choice",
      "prompt": "What is $\\operatorname{cot}\\frac{\\pi}{3}$ to three decimal places?",
      "choices": [
        "1.732",
        "0.866",
        "0.5",
        "0.577"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 3,
      "explanation": "$\\operatorname{cot}\\frac{\\pi}{3}=\\frac{1/2}{\\sqrt3/2}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt3}\\approx 0.577$."
    },
    {
      "id": "q9",
      "type": "fill_blank",
      "prompt": "The range of $y=\\tan x$ is \\_\\_.",
      "choices": [
        "all real numbers",
        "$[-1,1]$",
        "$[0,\\infty)$",
        "$(-\\pi,\\pi)$"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 0,
      "explanation": "Near an asymptote tangent grows without bound in both directions."
    }
  ]
}
